None. That's unanimous. Thank you so much. Moving right

52:50.845 --> 52:54.037
along onto the next one that's in relation to this one is the

52:54.061 --> 52:58.341
Code of Conduct amendment in relation to what we just heard

52:58.533 --> 53:02.397
so that we can look to rectify this

53:02.461 --> 53:06.225
issue. I will just like to,

53:06.965 --> 53:10.581
if you don't mind, take a moment but before I do

53:10.613 --> 53:14.415
I would need a mover and a seconder at least for Galler

53:14.495 --> 53:18.315
and Richardson. Okay, thank you. Not looking over you,

53:19.575 --> 53:22.711
thank you. And if you could just give me a moment, I would like to

53:22.743 --> 53:26.575
read this out loud in

53:26.615 --> 53:30.527
relation to the Integrity Commissioner report in which I self reported.

53:30.631 --> 53:34.247
I respectfully submit a resolution to council for consideration

53:34.431 --> 53:38.431
to remedy the Code of Conduct and these changes, if approved, will become applicable to

53:38.463 --> 53:41.921
all members of Council. Council the resolution has been crafted with

53:41.953 --> 53:45.365
input from the Integrity Commissioner and the City of Guelph Clerks Department

53:45.985 --> 53:50.145
in specific reference to the Global Covenant of mayors. In 2018,

53:50.305 --> 53:53.665
Guelph City Council unanimously approved Guelph becoming

53:53.745 --> 53:57.165
a signatory to this globally recognized organization.

53:58.185 --> 54:01.265
And in 2022 the Federation of Canadian

54:01.305 --> 54:05.771
Municipalities of which Guelph is a member, contacted me directly

54:05.953 --> 54:09.935
to ask if they could submit my name through them as the Secretariat

54:10.095 --> 54:13.543
to be considered as a position for the North American Representative on the

54:13.559 --> 54:17.287
GCOM Board of Directors. And I was unanimously approved to

54:17.311 --> 54:20.955
join. Now since that time I have represented. I have

54:21.335 --> 54:24.887
represented the GCOM values and goals while also representing

54:24.911 --> 54:28.399
the City of Guelph. As Mayor, I have attended several events

54:28.447 --> 54:32.351
to speak on the work our city is doing and advocate for the inclusion

54:32.383 --> 54:35.075
of cities within higher orders of government policies.

54:35.755 --> 54:39.651
My presence along GCOM has already secured $50,000

54:39.723 --> 54:43.371
US towards the creation of a new Youth Climate

54:43.483 --> 54:47.131
Action Fund which has been successfully launched

54:47.243 --> 54:50.459
and supported by young people across our city. In fact,

54:50.507 --> 54:53.651
I think some of the delegates here tonight are speaking from

54:53.683 --> 54:57.539
some of the money where that has gone. I am now currently

54:57.627 --> 55:02.451
working in the final stages of trying to secure $100,000

55:02.523 --> 55:05.891
US for a second round of grants for our youth

55:05.963 --> 55:08.575
in the city for Climate Change action.

55:09.635 --> 55:12.867
These connections have also led to successful training provided for

55:12.891 --> 55:15.507
City of Guelph staff through partnerships with ICLE,

55:15.611 --> 55:19.491
C40 Cities and GCOM enabling the opportunity to strengthen the

55:19.523 --> 55:23.027
impacts of our own Climate Change and Energy Office. Now,

55:23.051 --> 55:27.147
from a government relations perspective, I have continued to promote Guelph

55:27.211 --> 55:31.027
innovation, sustainable infrastructure projects, energy initiatives to upper levels

55:31.051 --> 55:34.493
of government. And I continue to advocate for greater municipal resources

55:34.549 --> 55:38.357
and supports for environmental projects and champion applications

55:38.421 --> 55:42.093
for funding for climate change initiatives. So this motion

55:42.149 --> 55:45.653
before us is to ensure that this matter can be resolved so that

55:45.669 --> 55:49.741
the important work on behalf of the city of Guelph and our partnerships with fcm,

55:49.893 --> 55:53.389
icle, the Cities for Climate Protection Network and GCOM

55:53.437 --> 55:57.341
can continue to proceed. And it's also consistent

55:57.373 --> 56:01.219
with the council and mayor expense policy regarding education programs

56:01.397 --> 56:05.319
and attendance at events. So with that, the motion as it

56:05.367 --> 56:08.775
