01:32:49.329 --> 01:32:52.649
the bill. We recovered, we submit it. We don't

01:32:52.697 --> 01:32:54.245
earn anything on that.

01:32:55.585 --> 01:32:58.665
The return is capped at a certain amount.

01:32:58.825 --> 01:33:02.873
If we happen to earn in any particular year a little bit more than that,

01:33:02.969 --> 01:33:06.513
we have to share it with the ratepayers and give them.

01:33:06.689 --> 01:33:10.551
If we had a super efficient

01:33:10.623 --> 01:33:14.695
year and save money somewhere and bumped up our return

01:33:14.775 --> 01:33:18.351
beyond a certain threshold above our regulated

01:33:18.423 --> 01:33:22.135
return, we would end up sharing the benefit with the ratepayers.

01:33:22.255 --> 01:33:26.039
So when you're talking about revenues and returns

01:33:26.087 --> 01:33:29.767
for the regulated utility, it is very

01:33:29.831 --> 01:33:33.431
regulated and restricted as to how much we can actually earn.

01:33:33.583 --> 01:33:37.125
So the numbers that are often mentioned when you talking about

01:33:37.165 --> 01:33:40.773
a billion dollars or whatever, that, as Mr. Costello was saying,

01:33:40.829 --> 01:33:45.173
is the total corporation, North American corporation,

01:33:45.269 --> 01:33:47.985
not the regulated Ontario utility.

01:33:51.165 --> 01:33:54.453
Thank you. And one last question. As a regulated company,

01:33:54.629 --> 01:33:58.197
you're regulated in terms of your rate of return. The way you grow your business

01:33:58.261 --> 01:34:02.125
