Thank you, Evan. Thank you for coming. You know the drill, so I'll

02:02:24.541 --> 02:02:28.117
turn it over to you. Great, thank you. Mr. Mayor and members of council,

02:02:28.181 --> 02:02:31.461
I'd just like to apologize for my bit of laughter earlier in the,

02:02:31.493 --> 02:02:35.253
in the, in the evening. It was disrespectful of council and the delegates and I

02:02:35.269 --> 02:02:38.597
apologize for that. The proposed motion

02:02:38.661 --> 02:02:42.277
that before you is a step to

02:02:42.301 --> 02:02:45.685
end a perverse fossil fuel subsidy paid. Paid by municipal

02:02:45.725 --> 02:02:49.489
taxpayers. As you know, the motion would ask the province to allow

02:02:49.537 --> 02:02:53.057
municipalities to charge fees to use

02:02:53.081 --> 02:02:56.273
our city owned roadways for gas pipelines.

02:02:56.449 --> 02:03:00.321
It would also instruct city staff not to enter into an agreement that would lock

02:03:00.353 --> 02:03:03.525
us into providing free access for 20 years.

02:03:04.065 --> 02:03:07.217
It's completely illogical that we're forced to provide free use of

02:03:07.241 --> 02:03:11.633
public lands to this gas company. First, we're missing out on significant revenue

02:03:11.769 --> 02:03:15.427
based on fees charged in other provinces. We estimate that

02:03:15.451 --> 02:03:18.935
Guelph would be earning $8.8 million per year.

02:03:19.395 --> 02:03:22.547
Second, by not receiving those fees, we are providing

02:03:22.611 --> 02:03:26.935
a major hidden subsidy to the methane gas system in Ontario.

02:03:27.315 --> 02:03:30.651
Burning methane gas contributes about one third of

02:03:30.683 --> 02:03:34.355
Ontario's greenhouse gas emissions. Taxpayers should not

02:03:34.395 --> 02:03:37.731
be subsidizing this climate destroying gas by giving this

02:03:37.763 --> 02:03:40.305
company free use of our public lands.

02:03:41.085 --> 02:03:45.109
Enbridge will tell you that they pay municipal taxes and

02:03:45.197 --> 02:03:48.585
somehow that makes them good corporate citizens.

02:03:49.805 --> 02:03:52.825
Anyone that owns property in Guelph pays taxes.

02:03:53.285 --> 02:03:57.157
Paying your municipal taxes is very different from paying for the use of public

02:03:57.221 --> 02:04:00.741
lands. And like many members of council here tonight,

02:04:00.893 --> 02:04:04.045
our household pays municipal taxes.

02:04:04.205 --> 02:04:08.027
But that doesn't allow me or any of you to

02:04:08.091 --> 02:04:11.575
build infrastructure for free on public lands.

02:04:11.875 --> 02:04:15.283
Taxes and land based fees for the use of public property

02:04:15.379 --> 02:04:19.035
are entirely different. The agreement Enbridge

02:04:19.115 --> 02:04:22.683
wants Guelph to sign would also force us to pay a significant portion

02:04:22.739 --> 02:04:26.643
of the cost of moving gas pipelines that conflict with our municipal

02:04:26.699 --> 02:04:30.455
infrastructure like sewers. This means that we could pay

02:04:30.795 --> 02:04:34.963
potentially millions of dollars when there is a conflict with gas pipelines that

02:04:34.979 --> 02:04:38.251
are paying nothing to use these lands. This is

02:04:38.283 --> 02:04:41.971
not fair and has been a major problem, a major infrastructure problem for

02:04:42.003 --> 02:04:46.547
other projects, including in the City of Toronto where the

02:04:46.571 --> 02:04:49.819
city had to pay up $14 million for the movement of

02:04:49.867 --> 02:04:53.055
certain infrastructure projects throughout the city.

02:04:53.475 --> 02:04:56.715
This agreement is totally unfair. By allowing free access for

02:04:56.755 --> 02:05:00.315
gas lines to these public lands and potentially charging taxpayers

02:05:00.355 --> 02:05:03.933
with these conflicts arise. If we want to truly

02:05:03.989 --> 02:05:07.813
reduce energy poverty, we shouldn't do that by subsidizing

02:05:07.869 --> 02:05:11.425
fossil fuels and should instead help residents

02:05:11.725 --> 02:05:15.509
install electric heat pumps, which are the cheapest

02:05:15.597 --> 02:05:19.341
way to heat homes. The city could use some of that revenue

02:05:19.373 --> 02:05:23.173
to increase the low income grants for heat pumps that the city already

02:05:23.269 --> 02:05:26.661
provides for low income people through the wonderful Guelph

02:05:26.693 --> 02:05:30.105
Greener Homes program. Then there's the city budget.

02:05:30.605 --> 02:05:34.165
We first became aware of this Enbridge franchise agreement when

02:05:34.205 --> 02:05:37.469
we heard that the Mayor had decided to cut the city budget by $15 million

02:05:38.261 --> 02:05:41.845
with almost every environmental program that the city funds

02:05:41.885 --> 02:05:45.157
on the chopping block. By passing this motion,

02:05:45.221 --> 02:05:48.877
Guelph would be joining municipalities who are also asking for the

02:05:48.901 --> 02:05:52.465
end to this subsidy, like the City of Toronto and the City of Ottawa.

02:05:52.815 --> 02:05:56.511
As the climate crisis continues to worsen. Let's be on the right side

02:05:56.543 --> 02:05:59.595
of history with this one small step forward.

02:06:00.655 --> 02:06:03.823
And to put a finer point on it, Guelph climate

02:06:03.879 --> 02:06:08.407
emissions jumped so much in 2022 that it amounted to overshooting

02:06:08.511 --> 02:06:11.555
the city's target by 17%.

02:06:12.055 --> 02:06:14.155
And emissions continue to rise.

02:06:15.215 --> 02:06:18.895
Emissions rising, cutting environmental

02:06:18.935 --> 02:06:22.133
budgets, giving subsidies to a multinational

02:06:22.189 --> 02:06:26.053
fossil fuel company that made a profit of $1.3 billion in

02:06:26.069 --> 02:06:28.745
the last quarter. Hmm.

02:06:29.845 --> 02:06:33.101
When thinking about this motion this evening and final decisions

02:06:33.133 --> 02:06:36.581
