I think that there's a lot of. If I

02:16:31.235 --> 02:16:34.779
may, Mr. Mayor, through you, I think there's a lot of platitudes in this motion

02:16:34.907 --> 02:16:38.297
that speak to trying to protect the rate payer, especially in

02:16:38.321 --> 02:16:42.257
this clause where we know definitively, I mean, we've even had the Clean Air

02:16:42.441 --> 02:16:45.481
alliance member state that the ratepayers will pay for this.

02:16:45.633 --> 02:16:48.321
So $8 million, if that's what's being charged to Enbridge,

02:16:48.353 --> 02:16:51.769
they'll simply put that into reserve fund, go back to the OEB at their next

02:16:51.817 --> 02:16:55.445
rate, review and pass that on to the rate payers.

02:16:57.585 --> 02:17:01.257
We are already experiencing energy poverty like never before in our province.

02:17:01.441 --> 02:17:04.583
In our country, we've seen G rates go up by almost 40% because of the

02:17:04.599 --> 02:17:08.247
carbon tax. I'm not looking to contribute to the energy

02:17:08.311 --> 02:17:11.795
poverty rates, especially for those people in marginalized housing or in

02:17:12.615 --> 02:17:15.967
housing insecurity. So I don't believe words

02:17:16.031 --> 02:17:19.687
and placation in some of these clauses do anything more

02:17:19.711 --> 02:17:23.195
than just try and put people's minds at ease. They won't work.

02:17:23.615 --> 02:17:27.287
This will be borne out by the rates and I'm

02:17:27.311 --> 02:17:31.617
not going to be contributing to that today. So. So those

02:17:31.641 --> 02:17:34.921
are just my thoughts, thank you. Okay, no problem. And Councillor Karan just wants to

02:17:34.953 --> 02:17:37.545
also bring comments to this one as well and then I'll call the vote.

02:17:37.625 --> 02:17:41.401
Yes, thank you. And these clauses are aspirational. I think we all Recognize that.

02:17:41.433 --> 02:17:44.425
But change is coming. It has to.

02:17:44.585 --> 02:17:48.121
We're in an energy transformation. And by stating that

02:17:48.153 --> 02:17:52.161
this is our aspirational goal, we're saying

02:17:52.233 --> 02:17:55.631
to the negotiation to the province and to the OED and

02:17:55.713 --> 02:17:59.515
to our fossil gas supplier, that we want to see

02:17:59.635 --> 02:18:03.131
change. The transfer of that, let's just say

02:18:03.163 --> 02:18:07.291
$8 million, because that's the figure that round we're

02:18:07.323 --> 02:18:11.095
talking about may indeed go to rate payers for

02:18:12.355 --> 02:18:15.859
gas customers, but that $8 million will also

02:18:15.907 --> 02:18:19.491
be revenue to the city. And then all members of

02:18:19.523 --> 02:18:23.095
the city aren't paying to subsidize the energy industry.

02:18:23.444 --> 02:18:27.504
And that $8 million can go to home energy loans,

02:18:27.964 --> 02:18:31.748
retrofits, utility bills,

02:18:31.796 --> 02:18:35.516
subsidies for low income families. There's a way to redistribute

02:18:35.580 --> 02:18:39.444
that money that benefits the people of Guelph rather than

02:18:39.604 --> 02:18:42.344
putting it on all of us equally through subsidization.

02:18:43.684 --> 02:18:47.332
Okay, thank you. So I will call number three then. If we could have it

02:18:47.348 --> 02:18:50.575
back up on the screen in its entirety.

02:18:50.695 --> 02:18:54.675
